  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "Public toilet seats have a gap at the front,",
      "start": 0.071,
      "end": 1.893
    },
    {
      "text": "and the one in your house almost certainly",
      "start": 2.157,
      "end": 3.533
    },
    {
      "text": "does not.",
      "start": 3.568,
      "end": 4.077
    },
    {
      "text": "It is written down.",
      "start": 4.224,
      "end": 4.938
    },
    {
      "text": "The plumbing codes most of the country builds",
      "start": 5.234,
      "end": 6.967
    },
    {
      "text": "to call for open-front seats in public restrooms,",
      "start": 7.003,
      "end": 9.165
    },
    {
      "text": "and have for over fifty years.",
      "start": 9.45,
      "end": 10.825
    },
    {
      "text": "The gap keeps the seat clear of the area",
      "start": 11.131,
      "end": 12.865
    },
    {
      "text": "you are most likely to touch while wiping,",
      "start": 12.955,
      "end": 14.616
    },
    {
      "text": "which matters far more when hundreds of strangers",
      "start": 14.815,
      "end": 16.887
    },
    {
      "text": "share one seat.",
      "start": 16.994,
      "end": 17.918
    },
    {
      "text": "It also leaves urine nowhere to pool.",
      "start": 17.971,
      "end": 19.543
    },
    {
      "text": "What reads as cost-cutting is a rule.",
      "start": 19.83,
      "end": 21.546
    }
  ],
